<h3>The delegation choreography</h3>
<p>Delegation is the most delicate behavior. The moment the model delegates, it does <em>not</em> go quiet. The sequence is:</p>
<ol style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:1.5rem;margin-bottom:.875rem">
  <li style="font-size:.925rem;color:var(--muted2);padding:.3rem 0;line-height:1.65">Model emits a brief holding reply: <em>"Let me look into that."</em></li>
  <li style="font-size:.925rem;color:var(--muted2);padding:.3rem 0;line-height:1.65">A hidden <code>&lt;/delegate&gt;</code> token dispatches the hard subtask to the background model.</li>
  <li style="font-size:.925rem;color:var(--muted2);padding:.3rem 0;line-height:1.65">The visual stream <em>keeps rolling</em> — the model stays present and continues watching.</li>
  <li style="font-size:.925rem;color:var(--muted2);padding:.3rem 0;line-height:1.65">The background result arrives (after a variable delay), and the model folds it into its next response.</li>
</ol>
<p>This is the "watch-and-do" loop: see something in the physical world, delegate a task into the digital world, and return with an answer — all without pausing the live stream.</p>
</section>

