    <h2>Audio Summary: JoyAI-VL-Interaction — The AI That Watches the World</h2>
    <p>JoyAI-VL-Interaction is a vision-language model that breaks from turn-based AI by continuously watching live video and deciding on its own, every second, whether to speak, stay silent, or delegate a hard task to a background model. Unlike Doubao, which polls every few seconds, or Gemini, which only responds when asked, JoyAI catches events — fires, falls, dart throws — the instant they happen. The key innovation is making the timing decision a native, learned capability of the model itself rather than an external trigger.</p>
    <p>The model is built on a compact 8B base using AdaCodec, which encodes predictable video frames in just 16 tokens versus 256 for full frames, keeping the context budget manageable over hours of streaming. Training uses over 4 million time-aligned clips where silence is a first-class label, and a weighted loss down-weights continued silence while up-weighting response onsets. A reinforcement learning stage with GRPO refines timing precision further. In head-to-head human evaluation across six real-world streaming scenarios, JoyAI wins 77.6% of comparisons against Doubao and 87.9% against Gemini, sweeping monitoring, counting, and translation at 100% win rates against Gemini.</p>
